.TH HIFIBERRY-OUTPUT-MODE 1 "August 2025" "HiFiBerry PipeWire" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hifiberry-output-mode \- control HiFiBerry output channel mapping
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hifiberry-output-mode
.RI { stereo | mono | left | right }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hifiberry-output-mode
controls the channel mapping of the HiFiBerry PipeWire output filter.
The filter is automatically inserted into the audio pipeline and provides
different output modes for stereo audio content.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B stereo
Normal left/right stereo output (default). Left channel goes to left output,
right channel goes to right output.
.TP
.B mono
Mix left and right channels equally and send to both outputs. Both outputs
will contain the same mono signal (L+R)/2.
.TP
.B left
Send only the left channel to both outputs. Right channel input is ignored.
.TP
.B right
Send only the right channel to both outputs. Left channel input is ignored.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B hifiberry-output-mode stereo
Set normal stereo operation (default)
.TP
.B hifiberry-output-mode mono
Mix both channels to mono output on both speakers
.TP
.B hifiberry-output-mode left
Play only left channel on both speakers
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/50-hifiberry-output-modes.conf
WirePlumber configuration that creates the output mode filter
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hifiberry-eq (1),
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR wireplumber (1)
.SH AUTHOR
HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>
